IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Control of Naval Waters Act 1918 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1918A00028.txt
-- (compilation No. 6, 21 October 2016). The master or owner of a vessel,
-- aircraft or vehicle asks: "Must I obey the superintendent's direction; must
-- I pay for the removal; when can my property be sold, and what do I get back
-- or still owe?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 2(1)-(2) exempt vessel.
DECLARE `Kind of craft` IS ONE OF
    `a vessel of the Commonwealth or the Australian Navy`
    `a foreign naval vessel declared exempt`
    `another vessel`
    `an aircraft`
    `a vehicle`

-- ss 6, 6A: where the craft is (naval waters are declared by Proclamation, s 3B).
DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `within naval waters`
    `on the foreshore of naval waters`
    `elsewhere`

DECLARE `Naval case` HAS
    `my craft`                                              IS A `Kind of craft`
    `where it is`                                           IS A `Place`
    -- ss 6(1), 6A(1)
    `I am in command or charge of it`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the superintendent gave me a direction about it`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I complied with the direction`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8
    `the superintendent moved or removed it under s 6(3), 6A(3) or 7` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commonwealth's expenses`                           IS A NUMBER
    `the demand for payment was made on`                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the expenses have been paid`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sale proceeds`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the expenses of the sale`                              IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Naval position` HAS
    `my craft is exempt`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `failing the direction is an offence`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum penalty units`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `I must pay the removal expenses on demand`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earliest day it may be sold at auction`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the surplus paid to me after a sale`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the deficiency I still owe after a sale`               IS A NUMBER

§ `Rules`

-- s 2(1) exempt vessel; s 2(2): references to a vessel exclude exempt vessels.
@ref s 2
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my craft is exempt` c IF
        c's `my craft` EQUALS `a vessel of the Commonwealth or the Australian Navy`
    OR  c's `my craft` EQUALS `a foreign naval vessel declared exempt`

-- s 6(1)-(2): a vessel within naval waters, its master. s 6A(1)-(2): an
-- aircraft, vehicle or vessel on the foreshore, the person in command or
-- charge. 10 penalty units; s 6(2A): strict liability.
@ref ss 6(1)-(2A), 6A(1)-(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction could lawfully be given` c IF
        NOT (`my craft is exempt` c)
    AND (   (    c's `where it is` EQUALS `within naval waters`
             AND c's `my craft` EQUALS `another vessel`)
         OR c's `where it is` EQUALS `on the foreshore of naval waters`)

@ref ss 6(2), 6A(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing it is an offence` c IF
        `the direction could lawfully be given` c
    AND c's `I am in command or charge of it`
    AND c's `the superintendent gave me a direction about it`
    AND NOT (c's `I complied with the direction`)

-- s 8(1): the owner must pay the expenses on demand.
@ref s 8(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must pay the expenses` c IF
        NOT (`my craft is exempt` c)
    AND c's `the superintendent moved or removed it under s 6(3), 6A(3) or 7`

-- s 8(3): "after the expiration of 3 months after the making of a demand":
-- the 3 months end on the corresponding day (the month's last day where there
-- is none), and a sale may be made from the next day.
@ref s 8(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest sale day for` c MEANS
    IF (NOT (`I must pay the expenses` c)) OR c's `the expenses have been paid`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `the demand for payment was made on`
         WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`add months` d 3 PLUS 1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total recoverable for` c MEANS
    c's `the Commonwealth's expenses` PLUS c's `the expenses of the sale`

-- s 8(5): any surplus is paid to the owner on demand; s 8(6): a deficiency is
-- recoverable as a debt.
@ref s 8(5)-(6)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surplus for` c MEANS
    IF `the earliest sale day for` c EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF c's `the sale proceeds` GREATER THAN `the total recoverable for` c
         THEN c's `the sale proceeds` MINUS `the total recoverable for` c
         ELSE 0

@ref s 8(6)
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deficiency for` c MEANS
    IF `the earliest sale day for` c EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the total recoverable for` c GREATER THAN c's `the sale proceeds`
         THEN `the total recoverable for` c MINUS c's `the sale proceeds`
         ELSE 0

@ref ss 2, 6, 6A, 8
@export default The position of the master, person in charge or owner of a vessel, aircraft or vehicle in or on the foreshore of naval waters under the Control of Naval Waters Act 1918 (Cth): whether the craft is exempt (Commonwealth, Navy or declared foreign naval vessels, s 2); whether failing to comply with the superintendent's direction about mooring, placing or removing it is an offence (ss 6(2), 6A(2): 10 penalty units, strict liability); whether the owner must pay the expenses of the superintendent moving or removing it (s 8(1)); the earliest day it may be sold at auction if unpaid 3 months after demand (s 8(3)); and the surplus paid back to the owner, or the deficiency still owed, after a sale (s 8(5)-(6)). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Naval case`  @desc My craft and where it is, any direction and whether I complied, and any removal, demand and sale
GIVETH A `Naval position`
`the naval position for` c MEANS
    `Naval position` OF `my craft is exempt` c, `failing it is an offence` c, (IF `failing it is an offence` c THEN 10 ELSE 0),
                        `I must pay the expenses` c, `the earliest sale day for` c, `the surplus for` c, `the deficiency for` c
